[[Al-Hilal Saudi FC|Al-Hilal]] became the third Asian club to reach the Club World Cup final in the 19th edition of the tournament. They are also the first [[Asian Football Confederation|AFC]] nominee to do so, as the Asian appearances in the [[2016 FIFA Club World Cup final|2016]] and [[2018 FIFA Club World Cup final|2018]] finals were both the club of the host association.<ref name="RSSSF">{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tablesf/fifawcc.html |title=FIFA Club World Cup |date=27 January 2023 |access-date=8 February 2023 |last1=Leme de Arruda |first1=Marcelo |last2=Di Maggio |website=[[RSSSF]] |first2=Roberto}}</ref>

Note: On 27 October 2017, [[FIFA]] officially recognised all the champions of the Intercontinental Cup as club world champions, in equal status to the FIFA Club World Cup.<ref name="FIFA2022">{{cite press release |date=27 October 2017 |title=FIFA Council approves key organisational elements of the FIFA World Cup |url=https://www.fifa.com/about-fifa/news/y=2022/m=10/news=fifa-council-approves-key-organisational-elements-of-the-fifa-world-cu-2917722.html |publisher=FIFA |access-date=27 October 2017}}</ref>
